{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1156265-two-questions-regarding-void-engineers","id":1156265,"title":"Two questions regarding Void Engineers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-06T02:40:02-08:00","id":1156265,"title":"Two questions regarding Void Engineers","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> NWO\u2019s Operations and the more jingoistic wire-heads in Iteration X eat up stories of the BCD\u2019s exploits. </div> </div> </div>Operations would probably be Operatives Methodology. But which are &quot;more jingoistic<i> wire-heads</i>&quot; referring? Shock Corps, crack troopers and other soldiers of the Machine Convention?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The EFD maintains all the Void Engineer-created constructs on Earth, including all deep-sea installations. This herculean task falls to the Maintenance and Custodial Division (\u201cScruffies\u201d). Its unsung heroes in grey jumpsuits somehow keep 16.52 million square feet of Consensus-defying real estate from being devoured by the oceans of the world. Given the incredible importance of these facilities \u2014 including Station Yemaja, and its delicate cargo of Paradox-vulnerable personnel and experiments. The Syndicate devotes an awe-inspiring amount of funding to its operations. </div> </div> </div>Do you think &quot;these facilities&quot; indicate each and every VE-created installation on the Earth? Or is &quot;the incredible importance&quot; statement solely limited to undersea Constructs such as Station Yemaja?<br /> <br /> Besides, why the post-Anomaly Union are so heavily relying on undersea facilities? Since, well, other far corners of the Earth, such as Polar Regions, jungles and deserts could house large scale Consensus-defying installations, with much cheaper build and maintenance costs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T06:35:43-08:00","id":1156320,"title":"","content":"I always took the undersea construct as the logical location due to astronauts zero gravity training being conducted under water. I saw this as an extension of that.<br /> <br /> Whether or not that still hold true I'm not sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T12:13:34-08:00","id":1156427,"title":"","content":"You could put your horrifically vulgar research station in the uninhabitable part of the Sahara or on the unfashionable end of the ice shelf on Antartica, but eventually some Sleeper plane or satellite will overfly it, and you'll spend too many resources modifying their memories and records each time. Put simply, nothing is so remote as the bottom of the ocean. <br /> <br /> Also, depending on your interpretation of Reality Zones, you might say that some remote areas still have some trace of human Consensus from past presence. If Roald Amundsen once walked through the godforsaken chunk of ice now housing your research, does some echo of his beliefs still exist there? No such trace exists in the Marianas Trench. <br /> <br /> Finally, there could be more mundane reasons. The surrounding ocean offers nigh-infinite cooling and garbage disposal, and a small self-destruct nuke might still go unnoticed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T01:26:58-08:00","id":1156613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1156265-two-questions-regarding-void-engineers?p=1156320#post1156320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always took the undersea construct as the logical location due to astronauts zero gravity training being conducted under water. I saw this as an extension of that.<br /> <br /> Whether or not that still hold true I'm not sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>VE are already owning plenty of such facilities - such as famous Star City. And those installations and training/launch sites are extensively dispersed on various continents. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haldir2012</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1156265-two-questions-regarding-void-engineers?p=1156427#post1156427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could put your horrifically vulgar research station in the uninhabitable part of the Sahara or on the unfashionable end of the ice shelf on Antartica, but eventually some Sleeper plane or satellite will overfly it, and you'll spend too many resources modifying their memories and records each time. Put simply, nothing is so remote as the bottom of the ocean.<br /> <br /> Also, depending on your interpretation of Reality Zones, you might say that some remote areas still have some trace of human Consensus from past presence. If Roald Amundsen once walked through the godforsaken chunk of ice now housing your research, does some echo of his beliefs still exist there? No such trace exists in the Marianas Trench.<br /> <br /> Finally, there could be more mundane reasons. The surrounding ocean offers nigh-infinite cooling and garbage disposal, and a small self-destruct nuke might still go unnoticed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you - that is a very thoughtful answer. But couldn't the Union easily conceal such locals via hypertech jamming and clocking. Sleeper planes or satellites have been incapable of detecting any Union installation, whether it is located at Earthside or Umbra. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},